WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.860 --> 00:00:03.500
There are so many new beauty products

00:00:03.500 --> 00:00:04.860
being released all the time,

00:00:04.860 --> 00:00:06.470
so we gathered some of the most hyped

00:00:06.470 --> 00:00:09.230
from the last month to test for ourselves.

00:00:09.230 --> 00:00:11.800
First up we have the
Madluvv Brow Stamp Kit

00:00:11.800 --> 00:00:13.450
that went viral on TikTok.

00:00:13.450 --> 00:00:16.440
It comes with five
different-sized brow stencils.

00:00:16.440 --> 00:00:18.860
You basically apply the
stencil to your brow

00:00:18.860 --> 00:00:21.440
and stamp the brow color on to fill.

00:00:21.440 --> 00:00:23.740
This was surprisingly easy to use,

00:00:23.740 --> 00:00:26.760
and it is kind of fun to,
like, stamp on a brow.

00:00:26.760 --> 00:00:28.185
I think I applied a little too much

00:00:28.185 --> 00:00:29.918
of the brow color, but
I liked how it looked

00:00:29.918 --> 00:00:32.470
after diffusing the
color with the spoolie.

00:00:32.470 --> 00:00:35.240
My brows are a little
sparse but naturally full,

00:00:35.240 --> 00:00:36.523
so I think a product like this

00:00:36.523 --> 00:00:37.898
is definitely better for people

00:00:37.898 --> 00:00:40.180
with little to no brow hair.

00:00:40.180 --> 00:00:42.438
I am so torn on my feelings

00:00:42.438 --> 00:00:43.988
for this Rimmel mascara.

00:00:43.988 --> 00:00:46.490
The brush is a very spiky plastic

00:00:46.490 --> 00:00:48.650
that kind of hurt my
eyes when I was applying.

00:00:48.650 --> 00:00:49.960
I didn't like that at all.

00:00:49.960 --> 00:00:51.810
And the actual mascara formula

00:00:51.810 --> 00:00:54.101
is so weird and gloopy,

00:00:54.101 --> 00:00:56.710
but after applying it, I think I liked it.

00:00:56.710 --> 00:00:59.280
It definitely lengthened my lashes a lot,

00:00:59.280 --> 00:01:00.921
and it didn't get too clumpy

00:01:00.921 --> 00:01:02.221
when I was layering it up.

00:01:02.221 --> 00:01:04.620
It didn't do too much for
me in terms of thickening,

00:01:04.620 --> 00:01:06.970
which is mainly what I
look for in a mascara.

00:01:06.970 --> 00:01:08.520
But if you're someone who wants length

00:01:08.520 --> 00:01:10.400
from a mascara, you'd like this.

00:01:10.400 --> 00:01:13.260
But be aware of the really spiky brush.

00:01:13.260 --> 00:01:15.430
Colourpop came out with
a new lipstick formula,

00:01:15.430 --> 00:01:17.310
the Glossy Lip Stain.

00:01:17.310 --> 00:01:19.260
I was kind of blown away by this.

00:01:19.260 --> 00:01:21.320
The color is so rich and vibrant.

00:01:21.320 --> 00:01:23.360
I don't know why I
expected it to be sheer,

00:01:23.360 --> 00:01:24.840
but it's definitely not.

00:01:24.840 --> 00:01:26.700
There was a slight
patchiness that went away

00:01:26.700 --> 00:01:28.570
with another swipe of the product.

00:01:28.570 --> 00:01:30.411
The texture is thinner

00:01:30.411 --> 00:01:31.870
than I would expect from a gloss

00:01:31.870 --> 00:01:34.011
and has a slightly tacky finish,

00:01:34.011 --> 00:01:35.170
which I didn't mind.

00:01:35.170 --> 00:01:37.750
And before it dries
down, it does transfer.

00:01:37.750 --> 00:01:39.500
Here's what it looked
like a few hours later

00:01:39.500 --> 00:01:41.010
when it was pretty dried down.

00:01:41.010 --> 00:01:43.100
The stain it leaves behind is so pretty

00:01:43.100 --> 00:01:45.420
and gives you those, like, Popsicle lips.

00:01:45.420 --> 00:01:46.360
Once it dries down,

00:01:46.360 --> 00:01:47.870
it's pretty transfer-proof.

00:01:47.870 --> 00:01:50.157
I love this, and I will definitely

00:01:50.157 --> 00:01:52.110
be buying some more shades.

00:01:52.110 --> 00:01:53.876
I love Melt Cosmetics,

00:01:53.876 --> 00:01:55.384
and I was totally mesmerized

00:01:55.384 --> 00:01:57.180
when I saw these new liquid highlighters

00:01:57.180 --> 00:02:00.360
they were releasing,
especially this pink one.

00:02:00.360 --> 00:02:02.130
I literally never wear pink highlighter,

00:02:02.130 --> 00:02:04.288
but this color was just speaking to me,

00:02:04.288 --> 00:02:05.620
and I had to have it.

00:02:05.620 --> 00:02:08.060
The glow these give is intense.

00:02:08.060 --> 00:02:10.110
It looks really good on bare skin.

00:02:10.110 --> 00:02:11.735
Not super natural,

00:02:11.735 --> 00:02:13.968
but not glittery or too metallic.

00:02:13.968 --> 00:02:15.970
I also love it over my foundation.

00:02:15.970 --> 00:02:17.228
It didn't break anything up,

00:02:17.228 --> 00:02:18.794
and it layered really well.

00:02:18.794 --> 00:02:20.410
You can also wear these on the body

00:02:20.410 --> 00:02:21.935
or mix them into your foundation

00:02:21.935 --> 00:02:23.260
to make it more glowy.

00:02:23.260 --> 00:02:24.726
These are pricey,

00:02:24.726 --> 00:02:26.717
but because you can wear
them in so many ways,

00:02:26.717 --> 00:02:28.740
I think it's worth it.

00:02:28.740 --> 00:02:31.930
I am so not a cream-bronzer
kind of person,

00:02:31.930 --> 00:02:33.600
but I've been seeing them everywhere.

00:02:33.600 --> 00:02:35.990
This one from E.l.f. has
been getting great reviews,

00:02:35.990 --> 00:02:38.460
and it's super affordable,
so I had to try it.

00:02:38.460 --> 00:02:40.400
The texture is hard to describe,

00:02:40.400 --> 00:02:42.833
because it blends from a cream to this

00:02:42.833 --> 00:02:47.090
supersoft diffused,
almost powderlike finish.

00:02:47.090 --> 00:02:48.940
What scares me about cream bronzer

00:02:48.940 --> 00:02:50.398
is it not being blendable

00:02:50.398 --> 00:02:52.410
and not meshing well with my foundation,

00:02:52.410 --> 00:02:54.160
but this one was so blendable

00:02:54.160 --> 00:02:55.401
and easy to work with,

00:02:55.401 --> 00:02:56.950
and you can definitely layer it

00:02:56.950 --> 00:02:58.342
if you want to build up the color.

00:02:58.342 --> 00:03:00.180
I love this.

00:03:00.180 --> 00:03:02.297
I had to get this Flower Beauty

00:03:02.297 --> 00:03:04.330
spray-can setting spray.

00:03:04.330 --> 00:03:06.900
I honestly thought this
was going to go terribly.

00:03:06.900 --> 00:03:08.470
You basically just shake it up

00:03:08.470 --> 00:03:11.000
and spray it all over your
face to set the makeup.

00:03:11.000 --> 00:03:12.870
Honestly, it wasn't that bad.

00:03:12.870 --> 00:03:15.600
It did set and matteify my face nicely.

00:03:15.600 --> 00:03:17.016
It didn't have a strong smell,

00:03:17.016 --> 00:03:18.082
which I was worried about,

00:03:18.082 --> 00:03:20.470
and it didn't spray powder everywhere.

00:03:20.470 --> 00:03:22.270
What I don't like about it is that

00:03:22.270 --> 00:03:25.070
it's hard to use in concentrated areas

00:03:25.070 --> 00:03:26.140
like my under-eyes.

00:03:26.140 --> 00:03:27.760
It didn't set that area very well,

00:03:27.760 --> 00:03:30.320
and I saw my concealer
creasing pretty quickly.

00:03:30.320 --> 00:03:32.160
I think this could be good for touch-ups,

00:03:32.160 --> 00:03:34.200
like getting rid of
oil throughout the day,

00:03:34.200 --> 00:03:36.720
but not for actually setting your makeup.

00:03:36.720 --> 00:03:38.180
Also, the spray is ...

00:03:38.180 --> 00:03:39.533
it's a little aggressive.

